course: dictionary
lesson: 2939
title: Dreamy and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dreamy» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a dreamy look or dreamy music. It has three main meanings: not paying attention, soft and gentle, or (informal) very attractive. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves, and the fall is over: a lazy beginning that suddenly turns into a wild, dreamy adventure.» The words «lazy» and «wild» show the story has moved into something strange, like a dream, so dreamy here means unreal and strange.
explain: «Alice heads for the March Hare's house... and walks up nervously: a strange, dreamy part, both funny and a bit creepy.» Again the clue is «strange». Swap in your meaning and check: does it still make sense? If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: «Dreamy» is an adjective: dreamier and dreamiest are its comparing forms.
fact: «Dreamy» can mean not paying attention, as if your mind is far away.
fact: «Dreamy» can mean soft, gentle and pleasant, like something in a dream, such as dreamy music.
fact: In informal speech, «dreamy» can mean very attractive or wonderful.
fact: Phrases to know: «a dreamy look», «dreamy music», «a dreamy adventure».
exercise: «She stared out of the window with a dreamy look.» What does dreamy mean here? | Dangerous and steep | Wet and grey | *Not paying attention, lost in her own thoughts | Very loud and busy
exercise: «The dreamy music filled the quiet room.» What does dreamy mean here? | Cold and wet | Fast and loud | *Soft, gentle and calm, like something in a dream | Broken and noisy
exercise: Jayden says, «Her new trainers are dreamy!» in a chat with friends. What does this informal use mean? | Lost in the woods | Sleepy after lunch | *Very attractive or wonderful | Frightened of the dark
test: In «a wild, dreamy adventure», what does dreamy suggest? | *Strange and unreal, like a dream | Heavy and wet | Very rude | Short and sharp
test: Which word means more dreamy, when you compare two things? | dream | *dreamier | dreamiest | dreamy
exam: Which meaning of dreamy fits «He gave a dreamy smile, as if he were far away»? | Freezing cold | *Thinking of other things, not paying attention | Very loud and cheerful | Sharp and pointed
